Author: Brian Olsen <bnolsen@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 20:33:29 2026 -0600

    fix(kernel): build on 7.3 -- ->create lost its bool excl argument
    
    Linux 7.3 dropped the trailing bool from inode_operations->create:
    
      int (*create)(struct mnt_idmap *, struct inode *, struct dentry *, umode_t);
    
    spadfs_create only gated the last argument on < 3.6 (nameidata vs excl),
    so on 7.3 the .create initialiser at namei.c:1169 failed with
    -Wincompatible-pointer-types and spadfs2.ko did not build on the running
    kernel. Add a < 7.3 bound on the excl argument. Neither nd nor excl is used
    in the body, so behaviour is unchanged.
    
    Verified: full spadfs2.ko build on 7.3.0_1 and 6.18.59_1, each with only
    the known MODULE_DESCRIPTION() warning; tests/mount_smoke.sh on 7.3.0_1:
    17 passed, 0 failed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/namei.c b/namei.c
index aa9e140..ba1b260 100644
--- a/namei.c
+++ b/namei.c
@@ -338,11 +338,11 @@ static int spadfs_create(
 			 struct mnt_idmap *ns,
 #endif
 			 struct inode *dir, struct dentry *dentry,
-			 mode_type mode,
+			 mode_type mode
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(3,6,0)
-			 struct nameidata *nd
-#else
-			 bool excl
+			 , struct nameidata *nd
+#elif LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(7,3,0)
+			 , bool excl
 #endif
 			 )
 {
